specific_instructions:
Respond with ONE JSON object only. No markdown, no code fences, no explanation. Shape:
{"operation": "<name>", "args": {...}}
Allowed operations:
- add_skill: args {"skill_name": "...", "experience_name": "...", "skill_level": 1-10 (optional)}
- update_skill_level: args {"skill_name": "...", "experience_name": "...", "skill_level": 1-10}
- delete_skill: args {"skill_name": "...", "experience_name": "..."}
- delete_all_skills: args {}
- none: args {}, plus "reason": "..." -- when no allowed operation fits the request
Rules: copy skill and experience names EXACTLY from the current data below. Choose the operation by what the request would DO to the data, not by its words: a request that removes skills or leaves the list shorter or empty is a deletion. Never invent an operation that is not in the list.

few_shot_examples:
Request: Add Rust to BRAINWORKS -> {"operation": "add_skill", "args": {"skill_name": "Rust", "experience_name": "BRAINWORKS"}}
Request: Remove Python from CSE 847 -> {"operation": "delete_skill", "args": {"skill_name": "Python", "experience_name": "CSE 847"}}
Request: Set my Python level in CSE 847 to 7 -> {"operation": "update_skill_level", "args": {"skill_name": "Python", "experience_name": "CSE 847", "skill_level": 7}}
Request: Remove every skill I have -> {"operation": "delete_all_skills", "args": {}}
Request: Rename my university -> {"operation": "none", "args": {}, "reason": "renaming institutions is not an allowed operation"}

specific_instructions:
Respond with ONE JSON object only. No markdown, no code fences, no explanation. Shape:
{"route": "<sql | semantic | semantic_then_sql | write | content>", "reason": "<one short line: why this route>", "steps": [<1 to 4 steps>]}
Each step is exactly one of:
{"expert": "Database Read Expert", "message": "<exact question>"}
{"expert": "Semantic Search", "query": "<words to look up>", "tables": ["<institutions|positions|experiences|skills>"]}
{"expert": "Database Write Expert", "message": "<the change>"}
{"expert": "Content Expert", "message": "<general question about the resume>"}
Rules:
1. Exact questions (counting, listing everything, totals, a name written exactly as stored) -> Database Read Expert only.
2. Abbreviations, nicknames, categories or vague wording (MSU, 'AI skills', 'my research job') -> Semantic Search. Search only the tables the question is about: skills -> ["skills"]; universities, companies, places -> ["institutions"]; jobs, roles -> ["positions"]; courses, projects -> ["experiences"]; unsure -> leave tables out.
3. If the user wants details about something that first has to be found by meaning, use Semantic Search first, then a Database Read Expert step. The second step automatically receives the search results.
4. Adding, changing, removing, clearing or emptying data, in ANY wording -> Database Write Expert. Pass the request on; never decide yourself whether it is allowed.
5. Only use the four expert names above.

few_shot_examples:
Request: How many skills do I have? -> {"route": "sql", "reason": "exact count", "steps": [{"expert": "Database Read Expert", "message": "How many skills do I have?"}]}
Request: List all my positions -> {"route": "sql", "reason": "list everything, no fuzzy words", "steps": [{"expert": "Database Read Expert", "message": "List all positions"}]}
Request: Find my MSU experience -> {"route": "semantic", "reason": "MSU is an abbreviation; stored name may differ", "steps": [{"expert": "Semantic Search", "query": "MSU", "tables": ["institutions"]}]}
Request: What data skills do I have? -> {"route": "semantic", "reason": "category, no skill is literally called data skills", "steps": [{"expert": "Semantic Search", "query": "data skills", "tables": ["skills"]}]}
Request: What did I do at UCLA? -> {"route": "semantic_then_sql", "reason": "resolve the abbreviation first, then look up positions there", "steps": [{"expert": "Semantic Search", "query": "UCLA", "tables": ["institutions"]}, {"expert": "Database Read Expert", "message": "List the positions at the institution found in the previous step"}]}
Request: Remove Python from CSE 847 -> {"route": "write", "reason": "the user wants to remove data", "steps": [{"expert": "Database Write Expert", "message": "Remove the skill Python from the CSE 847 experience"}]}
Request: Add Rust to BRAINWORKS -> {"route": "write", "reason": "the user wants to add data", "steps": [{"expert": "Database Write Expert", "message": "Add Rust as a skill to the BRAINWORKS experience"}]}
